WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.160
49 Manipur families each get 10 lack rupees for relatives missing since 2023. This is Omni

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:13.560
View Asia Pacific, Episode 10. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. The cabinet

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:17.860
signed off on Thursday, with Chief Minister Yunman Kim Jong-Sing in the chair.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:24.580
Spokesperson Sopam Ranjhan Singh called the payment a special humanitarian measure. Home Minister

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:30.280
Conthodrom Govindus told the assembly in September that fighting first between Kukizou and

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:36.300
Maytay communities, then between Kukiz and Naga's, killed 306 people and drove more than

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.780
60,000 from their homes.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:40.980
Singh said searches still have not found the 49.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:45.820
Families cannot collect the usual central death payment, because that scheme wants a

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:50.980
death certificate and an autopsy report, and the law treats a missing person as dead only

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:51.940
after seven years.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:01:02.540
The same meeting lifted payments for Army and Central Armed Police Forces personnel killed or hurt in extremist violence operations in the state, matching what state police already receive.

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:10.860
Death is now ten-lack rupees, permanent disability two-lack, agrivis injury one-lack, and a simple injury twenty thousand rupees.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:16.720
Those old figures, set in 2006, were two-lack for death and ten thousand for an injury.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:20.460
across the region, a Sydney teacher is now before the courts.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:25.080
Deandra Kantu, 32, was charged last week with nine offenses

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.300
over the alleged abuse of a teenage boy

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.500
during six months at Newington College,

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:31.500
the Sydney Morning Harold reports.

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:35.340
Most of what she is accused of happened in school hours at Stanmore,

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:37.380
where she taught as Harlem Beatis.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:42.080
The allegation followed a senior camp to Fitzroy Island on the Great Barrier Reef,

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:45.380
where she is accused of sexually touching the boy twice in the daytime

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:48.680
and sexually assaulting him between 10 and 11 at night.

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:52.160
Most of the charges are aggravated because she was his teacher.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:54.320
He told another teacher on the tour.

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:57.500
She was taken off the traveling party, later suspended,

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:00.500
and resigned when the school offered her a chance to explain.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:03.180
She had been there two years and left midterm.

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:06.400
Newington sent the allegation to New South Wales Police

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:08.420
and the Office of the Children's Guardian.

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:11.420
Detectives looked at it soon after the alleged abuse

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:15.000
then brought charges only after they restarted the case last year.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.960
On Thursday night, the school said the case is in court, and that it will keep

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:23.800
helping police. Yesterday's Asian Games Gold was in archery. Today, the new

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:29.540
result is in golf. Four-time PGA tour winner Kim Joo-hyeong shot a five-under-

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:34.540
65 on Friday at Kasugai Country Club, northeast of Nagoya, and he leads the

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:40.120
men's event by one stroke at 12-under-198 after 54 holes, young hop

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:46.180
reports. Wang Wei Shuang of Chinese Taipei and Kazuki Higa of Japan are the two names

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:52.200
one shot back. Team scoring adds each side's two best rounds. South Korea is at 20 under,

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:59.400
Japan at 19 under, and China and Chinese Taipei at 18 under. Kim is 24. Team mate Kim

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:05.200
Siyong Hyun is 28. A team gold or an individual gold would exempt either of them from military

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:05.940
military service.

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:09.320
Mundo Yobe, 34, has already done that duty.

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:12.300
He has tied for 8th at 8th under after a 69.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:20.660
Also today, Delhi police detained RJD MP Manoj Ja, AAP's Sarah Baradwaj and D.Y.F.I.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:25.440
activist, near Jontar Montaar, after refusing permission for a protest demanding that chief

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:28.720
election commissioner Ganesh Kumar resign, the Hindu reports.

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:33.780
In Queensland, an appeal court throughout Omar Segear's challenge to his convictions

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:39.400
for intentionally advocating terrorism, so he still faces two-and-a-half years ABC news reports.

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:45.700
Queensland police have also taken 558 illegal e-bikes and e-scooters in three months,

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:52.700
about six a day, and written 2,300 fines. In the wider world, Starbucks opened its first two

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:58.740
cafes in Uum Chi, in Xinjiang, on the 29th of September. Chinese state media welcomed them.

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:02.720
U.S. lawmakers and a Uyghur group did not, the Streets Times reports.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:07.780
John Moulinar, who chairs the U.S. House Select Committee on China, called the opening

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:12.640
morally bankrupt on the 1st of October and said it ties an American brand to the Chinese

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:14.940
Communist Party's campaign against Uyghurs.

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:20.220
The World Uyghur Congress said the company was looking past a dire human right situation,

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:25.800
and that firms should not feed an economy where state and post forced labor is still a serious

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:26.100
worry.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:32.100
The United Nations warned in 2022 of possible crimes against humanity there, including

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:35.700
detention of more than a million U.S. and other Muslim minorities.

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:40.880
Rights groups say serious abuses forced labor among them have not stopped.

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:46.480
Beijing denies the accusations and says its policies have rooted out extremism and brought

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:47.520
economic development.

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:52.680
The case on both sides of a deferred court visit is about who may speak to whom before

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:53.360
a law exists.

00:04:53.360 --> 00:05:00.400
A joint committee is studying the Constitution 129th Amendment bill of 2024 and a companion

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:05.340
bill on union territories. Together, they would set a framework for electing the Lok Sabha

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:09.840
and state assemblies at the same time. The bills went into the Lok Sabha in December

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:16.320
2024 and then to the committee, which BJP MPP P.P. Chaudhary chairs. The Hindu reports.

00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:21.640
The committee had wanted to visit the Supreme Court on 6 October for an informal talk

00:05:21.640 --> 00:05:26.980
with the Chief Justice and other judges about simultaneous elections. That visit is off.

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:32.460
The argument for holding it is the job of a committee. Look hard at a bill and take views from

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:36.360
experts and people with a stake. Committees have met sitting judges before.

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:41.020
Chargery's program cast the meeting as an informal discussion, not a hearing.

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:45.320
He later said members' dates did not line up and that he had other commitments.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:50.800
The argument against is the subject. Opposition members did not object to committees visiting

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:56.160
the court as such. They objected to sitting judges being asked about the merits or the constitutional

00:05:56.160 --> 00:06:01.480
validity of bills that could later be challenged in that same court. Independent Rajasabha

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:07.180
member Kapil Sabhal called the proposed talk unconstitutional. Parliament makes laws, he said,

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:12.520
and the judiciary tests whether those laws meet the constitution. Both sides accept that the

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:17.620
visit did not happen, and that the committee is still examining the two bills. Chaudhary has

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:22.740
blame the calendar. A sign of progress from the Nepal floods, one of 55 missing

